Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: StageRig
Upstream-Contact: Donnie Guedry <dguedry@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/dguedry/stagerig
Comment:
 The release tarball (stagerig-VERSION.tar.xz, made by
 scripts/make-source-tarball.sh) bundles the JUCE framework and the CLAP
 headers as git submodules. JUCE 8.0.15 is bundled because StageRig needs that
 release and the archive's juce-modules-source is older; the build uses the
 system CLAP headers (libclap-dev) and the bundled copy is a fallback for
 other distributions. The tarball leaves out JUCE's examples, tools and the
 AAX and ASIO SDKs, none of which a Linux build uses.
Files-Excluded:
 external/JUCE/examples
 external/JUCE/docs
 external/JUCE/extras/AudioPerformanceTest
 external/JUCE/extras/AudioPluginHost
 external/JUCE/extras/BinaryBuilder
 external/JUCE/extras/NetworkGraphicsDemo
 external/JUCE/extras/Projucer
 external/JUCE/extras/UnitTestRunner
 external/JUCE/extras/WindowsDLL
 external/JUCE/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/AAX/SDK
 external/JUCE/modules/juce_audio_devices/native/asio

